    "rawText": "Jane Doe\n123 -456 - 7890 | j ane . doe@example.com | l in ked in . com/in/j ane -doe | Seattle , WA\nEDUCATION\nUniversity of Washington Seattle, WA\nBS, Computer Science | GPA: 3.72/4.00 | Dean's List Sep. 2022 – Jun. 2026 (expected)\nEXPERIENCE\nSearch Infrastructure Co-op Seattle, WA\nFathomline Systems May 2025 – May 2026\n• Query latency in the autocomplete service spiked under load; adding a tiered LRU cache cut p99 latency from\n420ms to 85ms\n• Built a Rust-based indexing pipeline that reprocesses 30M documents nightly, replacing an 11 -hour full rebuild\nwith a 2-hour incremental one\n• Wrote a relevance-scoring harness that A/B tests ranking changes against 20 query sets before rollout\n• Traced a tokenizer bug that was silently dropping accented terms, recovering recall on roughly 5% of queries\n• Added query-shape validation to the ingestion API so malformed filters get rejected before hitting the index\nMobile App Lead Seattle, WA\nCascade Housing Cooperative Sep. 2024 – Jun. 2026\n• Rebuilt the co-op's iOS/Android app in React Native , cutting cold-start time from 3.8s to 1 .0s\n• Added offline sync with conflict resolution, cutting failed submissions during outages by roughly 85%\n• Shipped push notifications for maintenance updates, lifting resident response rate from 57% to 88%\n• Led 3 fellow student developers to ship a resident directory covering 950+ tenants, now averaging 4.6 stars\nacross app stores\nSecurity Contributor Seattle, WA\nHusky Security Collective Jan. 2024 – Jun. 2025\n• Ran a dependency audit across the co-op's stack, finding and patching 7 vulnerable packages before a\ndisclosed CVE went public\n• Added rate limiting and CSRF protection to the resident portal, closing 2 exploitable auth-bypass paths\n• Wrote a secrets-scanning pre-commit hook that's blocked 25+ accidental credential leaks since rollout\nPROJECTS\nPuzzle Solver Toolkit Feb. 2026 – present\nPython, NumPy | github.com/janedoe/puzzle-solver\n• Simulated annealing and A* search sit behind a shared heuristic interface for solving sliding-tile and Sokoban\npuzzles\n• Benchmarked 5 heuristics across 150 generated puzzles to compare solve time against optimality\n• Distributing search across worker processes cut median solve time roughly 3x\nTextbook Swap Marketplace Sep. 2024 – Dec. 2024\nReact, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Firebase | textbookswap.app\n• Peer-to-peer listings platform for textbook exchange, now used by 600+ students\n• Infinite scroll and image lazy-loading brought listing load time from 12s to 0.7s\n• An automatic matching system surfaces mutual-swap opportunities instead of requiring manual browsing\nSKILLS\nLanguages & Frameworks : Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, Java, SQL, React, Node.js\nTools : Docker, Git, CI/CD, PostgreSQL, Linux, AWS, Bash",
    "redactedText": "**** ***\n*** **** * **** | * *** * *************** * * ** *** ** * ******** *** **** * ******* * **\nEDUCATION\nUniversity of Washington Seattle, WA\nBS, Computer Science | GPA: 3.72/4.00 | Dean's List Sep. 2022 – Jun. 2026 (expected)\nEXPERIENCE\nSearch Infrastructure Co-op Seattle, WA\nFathomline Systems May 2025 – May 2026\n• Query latency in the autocomplete service spiked under load; adding a tiered LRU cache cut p99 latency from\n420ms to 85ms\n• Built a Rust-based indexing pipeline that reprocesses 30M documents nightly, replacing an 11 -hour full rebuild\nwith a 2-hour incremental one\n• Wrote a relevance-scoring harness that A/B tests ranking changes against 20 query sets before rollout\n• Traced a tokenizer bug that was silently dropping accented terms, recovering recall on roughly 5% of queries\n• Added query-shape validation to the ingestion API so malformed filters get rejected before hitting the index\nMobile App Lead Seattle, WA\nCascade Housing Cooperative Sep. 2024 – Jun. 2026\n• Rebuilt the co-op's iOS/Android app in React Native , cutting cold-start time from 3.8s to 1 .0s\n• Added offline sync with conflict resolution, cutting failed submissions during outages by roughly 85%\n• Shipped push notifications for maintenance updates, lifting resident response rate from 57% to 88%\n• Led 3 fellow student developers to ship a resident directory covering 950+ tenants, now averaging 4.6 stars\nacross app stores\nSecurity Contributor Seattle, WA\nHusky Security Collective Jan. 2024 – Jun. 2025\n• Ran a dependency audit across the co-op's stack, finding and patching 7 vulnerable packages before a\ndisclosed CVE went public\n• Added rate limiting and CSRF protection to the resident portal, closing 2 exploitable auth-bypass paths\n• Wrote a secrets-scanning pre-commit hook that's blocked 25+ accidental credential leaks since rollout\nPROJECTS\nPuzzle Solver Toolkit Feb. 2026 – present\nPython, NumPy | ********************************\n• Simulated annealing and A* search sit behind a shared heuristic interface for solving sliding-tile and Sokoban\npuzzles\n• Benchmarked 5 heuristics across 150 generated puzzles to compare solve time against optimality\n• Distributing search across worker processes cut median solve time roughly 3x\nTextbook Swap Marketplace Sep. 2024 – Dec. 2024\nReact, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Firebase | ****************\n• Peer-to-peer listings platform for textbook exchange, now used by 600+ students\n• Infinite scroll and image lazy-loading brought listing load time from 12s to 0.7s\n• An automatic matching system surfaces mutual-swap opportunities instead of requiring manual browsing\nSKILLS\nLanguages & Frameworks : Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, Java, SQL, React, Node.js\nTools : Docker, Git, CI/CD, PostgreSQL, Linux, AWS, Bash",
